<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/"
             xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/"
             xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/"
             xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/"
             id="Definitions_Greenbaum" name="GreenbaumScreen"
             namespace="http://harper.health/dmn/greenbaum">

  <inputData id="ID_brokenbones" name="historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts">
    <description>Subquestion 1a: history of broken bones or cuts needing stitches? Scored only when screenVariant is &quot;original&quot;; ignored under the modified tool.</description>
    <variable id="var_brokenbones" name="historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_knockedout" name="historyOfKnockedUnconscious">
    <description>Subquestion 1b: history of being knocked unconscious (&quot;knocked out&quot;)? Scored under both variants.</description>
    <variable id="var_knockedout" name="historyOfKnockedUnconscious" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_runaway" name="historyOfRunningAway">
    <description>History of running away from home?</description>
    <variable id="var_runaway" name="historyOfRunningAway" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_alcohol" name="historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse">
    <description>History of alcohol or drug abuse (past year)?</description>
    <variable id="var_alcohol" name="historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_law" name="everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement">
    <description>Ever involved with law enforcement?</description>
    <variable id="var_law" name="everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_std" name="historyOfSTD">
    <description>History of sexually transmitted disease?</description>
    <variable id="var_std" name="historyOfSTD" typeRef="boolean" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_partners" name="numberOfSexualPartners">
    <description>Number of sexual partners; counts as a positive item when greater than five.</description>
    <variable id="var_partners" name="numberOfSexualPartners" typeRef="number" />
  </inputData>
  <inputData id="ID_variant" name="screenVariant">
    <description>Which scoring variant to apply: &quot;original&quot; or &quot;modified&quot;. Defaults to modified when null or unrecognised.</description>
    <variable id="var_variant" name="screenVariant" typeRef="string" />
  </inputData>

  <decision id="Decision_Greenbaum" name="atRisk">
    <description>Screening Tool of Greenbaum. Short Screen for Child Sex Trafficking (SSCST). Positive ("At risk?") when two or more of the six items are positive; the partner item counts positive when the number of partners exceeds five. TWO VARIANTS. The original screen scores significant trauma as one item answered by two subquestions -- broken bones/cuts needing stitches (1a) and knocked unconscious (1b) -- where a yes to either counts once. The multi-site evaluation also tested a MODIFIED tool that drops 1a and scores trauma on 1b alone. Set screenVariant to "original" or "modified"; anything else, including omitting it, is treated as "modified". Harper defaults to modified. PERFORMANCE AT CUTOFF &gt;= 2 (Greenbaum VJ et al., J Adolesc Health 2018; n=810 across 16 sites). Modified (Harper default) -- emergency department: sensitivity 83.3%, specificity 59.5%, PPV 23.8%, NPV 95.9%; total sample: sensitivity 84.4%, specificity 64.6%, PPV 23.0%, NPV 97.1%. Original -- emergency department: sensitivity 83.3%, specificity 49.4%, PPV 20.0%, NPV 95.1%; total sample: sensitivity 84.4%, specificity 57.5%, PPV 19.9%, NPV 96.7%. Dropping 1a buys about 10 points of specificity in the ED at no cost to sensitivity, which is why it is the default. The ED figures are the ones applicable to Harper. The original single-site study (Greenbaum VJ, Dodd M, McCracken C, Pediatric Emergency Care, PMID 26599463) reported sensitivity 92.3%, specificity 74.4% -- better than either multi-site result; do not quote it as Harper's expected performance. Even at 59.5%, specificity means roughly 40% of non-victims screen positive: expect a high false-positive rate and staff the downstream referral path accordingly.</description>
    <variable id="var_atRisk" name="atRisk" typeRef="boolean" />
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_1"><requiredInput href="#ID_brokenbones" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_2"><requiredInput href="#ID_knockedout" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_3"><requiredInput href="#ID_runaway" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_4"><requiredInput href="#ID_alcohol" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_5"><requiredInput href="#ID_law" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_6"><requiredInput href="#ID_std" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_7"><requiredInput href="#ID_partners" /></informationRequirement>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_gb_8"><requiredInput href="#ID_variant" /></informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="le_greenbaum">
      <text>(
  (if screenVariant = "original"
     then (if historyOfBrokenBonesOrCuts = true or historyOfKnockedUnconscious = true then 1 else 0)
     else (if historyOfKnockedUnconscious = true then 1 else 0))
  + (if historyOfRunningAway = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfAlcoholOrDrugAbuse = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if everInvolvedWithLawEnforcement = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if historyOfSTD = true then 1 else 0)
  + (if (numberOfSexualPartners != null) and (numberOfSexualPartners > 5) then 1 else 0)
) >= 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>

  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram id="DMNDiagram_Greenbaum">
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_dec" dmnElementRef="Decision_Greenbaum">
        <dc:Bounds x="640" y="60" width="220" height="80" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb1" dmnElementRef="ID_brokenbones">
        <dc:Bounds x="60" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb2" dmnElementRef="ID_knockedout">
        <dc:Bounds x="250" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb3" dmnElementRef="ID_runaway">
        <dc:Bounds x="440" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb4" dmnElementRef="ID_alcohol">
        <dc:Bounds x="630" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb5" dmnElementRef="ID_law">
        <dc:Bounds x="820" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb6" dmnElementRef="ID_std">
        <dc:Bounds x="1010" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb7" dmnElementRef="ID_partners">
        <dc:Bounds x="1200" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="DMNShape_gb8" dmnElementRef="ID_variant">
        <dc:Bounds x="1390" y="300" width="160" height="60" />
      </dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb1" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_1"><di:waypoint x="140" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="660" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb2" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_2"><di:waypoint x="330" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="685" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb3" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_3"><di:waypoint x="520" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="710" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb4" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_4"><di:waypoint x="710" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="735" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb5" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_5"><di:waypoint x="900" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="760" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb6" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_6"><di:waypoint x="1090" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="785" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb7" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_7"><di:waypoint x="1280" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="810" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
      <dmndi:DMNEdge id="DMNEdge_gb8" dmnElementRef="ir_gb_8"><di:waypoint x="1470" y="300" /><di:waypoint x="835" y="140" /></dmndi:DMNEdge>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
